  "worked_solution": "To compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \u27e81,2\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\u27e8\\int 1\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 2\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8t+{C}_{1},2t+{C}_{2}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(1)=\u27e84,3\u27e9.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\u27e81+{C}_{1},2(1)+{C}_{2}\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e84,3\u27e9 & =\u27e81+{C}_{1},2+{C}_{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =1+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =2+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\nv=\u27e8t+3,2t+1\u27e9.\n$$",
